{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","data":{"alias":"genuine-sunbeamed-solitaire","creation_channel":"cli","description":"The archive-massgov-pfml checks entry runs the whole jest suite on every agent run, though its own comment claims only the tests covering the changed page run. A pre-existing date-dependent failure in tests/features/status/PaymentIntroPrepaidCard.test.tsx, unrelated to any agent diff, therefore failed CI for execution intake-f6f13c6b. The repair loop spent 105 LLM calls and 3.2M tokens trying to fix a test the agent did not touch, exhausted the budget, and parked the ticket in AWAITING_HUMAN with finished, correct work on the branch.\n\nThe platform declares no build-tool convention, so it must not choose a test selector. Instead it should tell the project which paths changed and let the project's declared command decide. Thread the ticket file_impact paths from the workflow into the checks activity and the checks pod, expose them to the declared command as a CHANGED_PATHS environment variable, and update the archive-massgov-pfml entry to pass them to jest --findRelatedTests with a full-suite fallback when the variable is empty.\n\nVerified against the promoted branch: jest --findRelatedTests over the five file_impact paths selects exactly the three suites the change affects, all of which pass, and excludes the unrelated failure.","id":"4d60-84ad-3b34-4d47","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["ci","checks"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Scope project checks to the changed paths"},"env_id":"8c3ef925-fbdc-4d88-8d59-f391cf59568c","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1789950703777878001,"uuid":"270ddbad-14e2-4380-8c50-8510bb5fa5f9"}